#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:5
#: 1de957f9512b4da0af6139a3b2c94670
msgid "Adding a New Flight Mode to Copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:7
#: fca6ee1396f642c8b0fe64a4a8740653
msgid "This section covers the basics of how to create a new high level flight mode (i.e. equivalent of Stabilize, Loiter, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:9
#: f130d41668df47abb5c3c421af051c3a
msgid "As a reference the diagram below provides a high level view of Copter's architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:15
#: 9b9ec5bd54a74cdd862f86188637565e
msgid "Pick a name for the new mode and add it to the bottom of the control_mode_t enum in `mode.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode.h#L14>`__ just like \"NEW_MODE\" has been added below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:48
#: 1388832d82e544d2a6546ff5a452334c
msgid "Define a new class for the mode in `mode.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode.h>`__. It is probably easiest to copy a similar existing mode's class definition and just change the class name (i.e. copy and rename \"class ModeStabilize\" to \"class ModeNewMode\"). The new class should inherit from the Mode class and implement ``run()``, ``name()`` and ``name4()`` and optionally ``init()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:64
#: 6381c39799d746ffa6e7674e8d0b2874
msgid "The ``name()`` and ``name4()`` methods are for logging and display purposes.  ``init()`` will be called when the vehicle first switches into this new mode so it should implement any required initialisation.  ``run()`` will be called at 400hz and should implement any pilot input decoding and then set position and attitude targets (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:66
#: 998bde87f25440c38a680eafa1f14a83
msgid "There are also some simple methods returning true/false that you may want to override that control features such as whether the vehicle can be armed in the new mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:75
#: fecb209375ab41ea9294c8a585e9355b
msgid "Create a new mode_<new flight mode>.cpp file based on a similar mode such as `mode_stabilize.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode_stabilize.cpp>`__ or `mode_loiter.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode_loiter.cpp>`__. This new file should probably implement the ``init()`` method which will be called when the vehicle first enters the mode.  This function should return true if it is OK for the vehicle to enter the mode, false if it cannot. Below is an excerpt from `mode_rtl.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode_rtl.cpp>`__'s init method that shows how the vehicle cannot enter RTL mode unless the home position has been set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:100
#: 1645ebe1df3e408bb7e9118bedfdc1e1
msgid "Below is an excerpt from `mode_stabilize.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode_stabilize.cpp>`__'s run method (called 400 times per second) that decodes the user's input, then sends new targets to the attitude controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:121
#: fb852451c5384f80b8368283e4387a88
msgid "Instantiate the new mode class in `Copter.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Copter.h#L894>`__ by searching for \"ModeAcro\" and then adding the new mode somewhere below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:142
#: 84c702854afe40a791797a679ad32754
msgid "In `mode.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/mode.cpp>`__ add the new mode to the ``mode_from_mode_num()`` function to create the mapping between the mode's number and the instance of the class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:160
#: b359c9f547254bdcb8e3986493129026
msgid "Add the new flight mode to the list of valid ``@Values`` for the ``FLTMODE1 ~ FLTMODE6`` parameters in `Parameters.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp#L262>`__ (Search for \"FLTMODE1\").  Once committed to master, this will cause the new mode to appear in the ground stations list of valid modes. Note that even before being committed to master, a user can setup the new flight mode to be activated from the transmitter's flight mode switch by directly setting the FLTMODE1 (or FLTMODE2, etc) parameters to the number of the new mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apmcopter-adding-a-new-flight-mode.rst:179
#: 28a1e0b3df2542259a2ca2f41220db7a
msgid "Optionally you may wish to add the flight mode to the ``COPTER_MODE`` enum within the `mavlink/ardupilotmega.xml <https://github.com/ArduPilot/mavlink/blob/master/message_definitions/v1.0/ardupilotmega.xml#L1027>`__ because some ground stations may use this to automatically populate the list of available flight modes."
msgstr ""
